Provides: zsys (= ${binary:Version}),
Conflicts: zsys,
Replaces: zsys,
Description: ZFS SYStem integration for any ZFS packaging
 ZSYS is a Zfs SYStem tool targetting an enhanced ZOL experience.
 It allows running multiple ZFS system in parallels on the same machine,
 get automated snapshots, managing complex zfs dataset layouts separating
 user data from system and persistent data, and more.
 .
 This build drives ZFS through the zfs and zpool commands instead of linking
 libzfs, so it works with Ubuntu's ZFS packages as well as upstream OpenZFS
 packages and future OpenZFS releases. It replaces the zsys package.
